unch.com/2013/08/27/arm-acquires-internet-of-things-startup-sensinode-to-move-beyond-tablets-and-phones/|title=ARM Acquires Internet Of Things Startup Sensinode To Move Beyond Tablets And Phones|publisher=AOL|work=TechCrunch|date=27 August 2013 |access-date=15 March 2015}}&lt;/ref>\n: Cadence&apos;s PANTA family of high-resolution display processor and scaling coprocessor IP cores (formerly developed in Evatronix)&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.arm.com/about/newsroom/arm-acquires-advanced-display-technology-from-cadence.php|title=ARM Acquires Advanced Display Technology from Cadence|website= arm.com| publisher= ARM Holdings |access-date=15 March 2015}}&lt;/ref>\n",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"no col break","href":"./Template:No_col_break"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n;2014\n: [[mbed TLS|PolarSSL]], a [[software library]] implementing the [[Secure Sockets Layer|SSL]] and [[Transport Layer Security|TLS]] protocols.&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://polarssl.org/tech-updates/blog/polarssl-part-of-arm |title=PolarSSL is now a part of ARM |first= Paul| last= Bakker |date=24 November 2014|website=Polar SSL|access-date=15 March 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141124143241/https://polarssl.org/tech-updates/blog/polarssl-part-of-arm |archive-date=24 November 2014}}&lt;/ref> (In February 2015, PolarSSL has been rebranded to [[mbed TLS]] to better show its fit inside the [[mbed]] ecosystem.&lt;ref name=rebranded>{{cite web|url=https://polarssl.org/tech-updates/releases/mbedtls-1.3.10-released|title=mbed TLS 1.3.10 released|date=8 February 2015 |website=PolarSSL |first1= Paul |last1=Bakker |access-date=9 February 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150209180352/https://polarssl.org/tech-updates/releases/mbedtls-1.3.10-released|archive-date=9 February 2015|url-status=dead}}&lt;/ref>)"}},"i":1}},"\n: [[Duolog]] Technologies, an [[electronic design automation]] company that developed a suite of tools that automate the process of IP configuration and IP integration&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.arm.com/about/newsroom/arm-concludes-its-acquisition-of-duolog-technologies.php|title=ARM Concludes its Acquisition of Duolog Technologies|date=1 August 2014|website= arm.com | publisher= ARM Holdings | access-date= }}&lt;/ref>\n",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"no col break","href":"./Template:No_col_break"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n;2015\n: Sansa Security, a provider of hardware security [[intellectual property]] (IP) and software for advanced system-on-chip components deployed in Internet of Things (IoT) and mobile devices&lt;ref>{{Cite press release|date=30 July 2015|title=ARM Expands IoT Security Capability with Acquisition of Sansa Security|url=https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20150729006920/en/ARM-Expands-IoT-Security-Capability-with-Acquisition-of-Sansa-Security|access-date=2 December 2020|website= businesswire.com|language=en}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":2}},"\n: Wicentric, a [[Bluetooth]] Smart stack and profile provider&lt;ref name=\"arm.com\">{{cite web|url=https://www.arm.com/about/newsroom/arm-announces-acquisition-of-wicentric-and-sunrise-micro-devices.php|title=ARM Announces Acquisition of Wicentric and Sunrise Micro|date=16 April 2015|website= arm.com | publisher= ARM Holdings | access-date= }}&lt;/ref>\n: Sunrise Micro Devices, a provider of sub-one volt Bluetooth radio intellectual property (IP)&lt;ref name=\"arm.com\"/>\n: Offspark, a provider of IoT security software&lt;ref>{{Cite web|title = ARM buys Leading IoT Security Company Offspark as it Expands its mbed Platform |url = https://www.arm.com/about/newsroom/arm-buys-leading-iot-security-company-offspark-as-it-expands-its-mbed-platform.php |date=9 February 2015 |website= arm.com | publisher= ARM Holdings |access-date=6 January 2016}}&lt;/ref>\n: Carbon Design Systems, a provider of cycle-accurate virtual prototyping solutions&lt;ref>{{Cite web|title = ARM to Offer Cycle-Accurate Virtual Prototyping for Complex SoCs Through an Asset Acquisition from Carbon Design Systems |url = https://www.arm.com/about/newsroom/arm-to-offer-cycle-accurate-virtual-prototyping-for-complex-socs-through-an-asset-acquisition-from.php |date=20 October 2015 |website= arm.com | publisher= ARM Holdings | access-date= 6 January 2016}}&lt;/ref>\n: On 19 November, ARM, alongside [[Cisco Systems]], [[Dell]], [[Intel]], [[Microsoft]], and [[Princeton University]], founded the [[OpenFog Consortium]], to promote interests and development in [[fog computing]].&lt;ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/janakirammsv/2016/04/18/is-fog-computing-the-next-big-thing-in-internet-of-things/2/#1971ac3a34c9 |title=Is Fog Computing the Next Big Thing in the Internet of Things? |last=Janakiram |first=MSV |date=18 April 2016|work= [[Forbes (magazine)|Forbes]] |access-date=18 April 2016}}&lt;/ref>\n;2016\n: Apical, a provider of imaging and embedded computer vision IP products&lt;ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.apical.co.uk/2016/05/18/arm-acquires-apical-a-global-leader-in-imaging-and-embedded-computer-vision/|title=ARM Acquires Apical – a Global Leader in Imaging and Embedded Computer Vision|last=Andrew|date=18 May 2016|website=Apical|access-date=20 July 2016}}&lt;/ref>\n: Allinea Software, a leading provider of software tools for HPC&lt;ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.arm.com/about/newsroom/arm-extends-hpc-offering-with-acquisition-of-software-tools-provider-allinea-software.php|title=ARM extends HPC offering with acquisition of software tools provider Allinea Software|website= arm.com | publisher= ARM Holdings| date=16 December 201| access-date= }}&lt;/ref>\n;2018\n: [[Treasure Data]] ($600 million acquisition), provides enterprise data management software for device-to-data IoT platform&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-07-29/softbank-owned-arm-is-said-to-agree-to-buy-u-s-s-treasure-data|title=SoftBank-Owned ARM Is Said to Agree to Buy Treasure Data |date=29 July 2018|website=Bloomberg}}&lt;/ref>\n: Stream Technologies, provided connectivity management platform and GSM connectivity&lt;ref>{{cite press release|url=https://www.arm.com/company/news/2018/06/arm-expands-iot-connectivity-and-device-management-capabilities-with-stream-technologies-acquisition|title=Arm Expands IoT Connectivity and Device Management Capabilities with Stream Technologies Acquisition|date=12 June 2018|publisher=ARM Holdings| website= arm.com | access-date= }}&lt;/ref>\n;2019\n: WigWag, an IoT gateway and cloud platform business&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://tracxn.com/d/acquisitions/acquisitionsbyArm|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20230721024647/https://tracxn.com/d/acquisitions/acquisitionsbyArm|url-status=dead|archive-date=21 July 2023|title=Acquisitions by Arm|date=20 July 2023|website=tracxn.com}}&lt;/ref>\n;2020\n: In July 2020, Arm announced plans to spin off Treasure Data, together with the other parts of its \"IoT Services Group\" business, into separate SoftBank-owned entities by the end of September 2020.&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.zdnet.com/article/arm-proposes-spinning-off-iot-businesses-into-new-softbank-owned-entities/|title=Arm proposes spinning off IoT businesses into new Softbank-owned entities|website=[[ZDNet]] |last= Condon| first= Stephanie|date=7 July 2020|access-date=13 July 2020}}&lt;/ref>\n;2025\n: August: [[Cadence Design Systems]] completed the acquisition of Arm Artisan Foundation IP, which ARM originally acquired from Artisan Components in 2004.&lt;ref name=\"YahooFinanceCadenceArmArtisan2025\">{{cite web |title=Cadence Completes Acquisition of Arm Artisan Foundation IP Business |url=https://finance.yahoo.com/news/cadence-completes-acquisition-arm-artisan-130000021.html |website=Yahoo Finance |agency=Business Wire |date=27 August 2025 |access-date=12 February 2026 |language=en }}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref name=\"ElectronicsWeeklyBusiness864157\">{{cite web |title=Arm selling Artisan physical IP unit to Cadence |url=https://www.electronicsweekly.com/news/business/864157-2025-04/ |last=Manners | first=David |website=Electronics Weekly |date=18 April 2025 |access-date=12 February 2026 |language=en }}&lt;/ref>\n",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"div-col-end","href":"./Template:Div-col-end"},"params":{},"i":3}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1184024115" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt108" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Div col/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .div-col{margin-top:0.3em;column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .div-col-small{font-size:90%}.mw-parser-output .div-col-rules{column-rule:1px solid #aaa}.mw-parser-output .div-col dl,.mw-parser-output .div-col ol,.mw-parser-output .div-col ul{margin-top:0}.mw-parser-output .div-col li,.mw-parser-output .div-col dd{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid-column}</style></span><div class="div-col   " about="#mwt107" id="mw1g">

<dl><dt>1999</dt>
<dd>Micrologic Solutions, a software consulting company based in Cambridge<sup about="#mwt111" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-27" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-27"}}'><a href="#cite_note-27" id="mw1w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2Q">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2g">]</span></span></a></sup></dd>
